{{also|partí|partì|partî|pårti|părți}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|parti}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpɑːti/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/pɑɹˈtiː/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The basic, central, or main [[concept]], [[drawing]], or [[scheme]] of an [[architectural]] [[design]].
# {{lb|en|dated}} Someone (especially a man) who is considered to be a good choice for [[marriage]], because of wealth, status etc.
#* '''1897''', Bram Stoker, ''Dracula'', [http://www.gutenberg.org/files/345/345-h/345-h.htm Chapter 5]:
#*: We met some time ago a man that would just do for you, if you were not already engaged to Jonathan. He is an excellent '''''parti''''', being handsome, well off, and of good birth.
#*'''1911''', {{w|Max Beerbohm}}, ''Zuleika Dobson'':
#*:“My temper is sweet, and my character without blemish. In fine, Miss Dobson, I am a most desirable '''parti'''.”

===Anagrams===
* {{l|en|tapir}}

